    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">20 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Length-prefix framing</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Design</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/encode-and-decode-strings/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 271</a> <span class=\"chip warn\">Premium</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Encode and Decode Strings</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Never trust a delimiter that can appear in the data. Write each string as <code>&lt;length&gt;#&lt;bytes&gt;</code>: the decoder reads the digits up to the first <code>#</code>, then takes exactly that many characters, so any character (even <code>#</code> or digits) inside a string is safe. O(total length) both ways.</p>\n"
  },
